Where are the push, pop, slice, shift, and unshift methods used when accessing array elements?  

| Method      | What it does                           | Works on     | Changes original array? |
| ----------- | -------------------------------------- | ------------ | ----------------------- |
| `push()`    | Adds element(s) at the **end**         | End          | ✅ Yes                   |
| `pop()`     | Removes element from the **end**       | End          | ✅ Yes                   |
| `unshift()` | Adds element(s) at the **beginning**   | Beginning    | ✅ Yes                   |
| `shift()`   | Removes element from the **beginning** | Beginning    | ✅ Yes                   |
| `slice()`   | Copies/extracts a portion              | Any position | ❌ No                    |

push example
let fruits = ["apple", "banana"];
fruits.push("orange");
console.log(fruits);
output = ["apple", "banana", "orange"]

pop example
let fruits = ["apple", "banana", "orange"];
fruits.pop();
console.log(fruits);
output = ["apple", "banana"]

unshift
let fruits = ["banana", "orange"];
fruits.unshift("apple");
console.log(fruits);
output = ["apple", "banana", "orange"]

shift
let fruits = ["apple", "banana", "orange"];
fruits.shift();
console.log(fruits);
output = ["banana", "orange"]

slice
let fruits = ["apple", "banana", "orange", "mango"];
let result = fruits.slice(1, 3);
console.log(result);
output = ["banana", "orange"]

whats the difference between slice and splice
slice() → extracts elements without changing the original array.
splice() → adds/removes/replaces elements and changes the original array.

splice
let arr = [10, 20, 30, 40];
arr.splice(1, 2);
console.log(arr);
// [10, 40]